# Course Offline Replay

Use when running `tools/student_replay.py --lab <lab> --runtime "$REPLAY_ENV"` for course labs.

## Procedure

1. Confirm `.venv/bin/python` exists: `ls /home/angel/Documents/Cyber_IA/.venv/bin/python`
2. Check `PYTHONPATH` includes `course_llm`: `PYTHONPATH=/home/angel/Documents/Cyber_IA:$PYTHONPATH`
3. Set runtime: `export REPLAY_ENV=/home/angel/Documents/Cyber_IA/.venv`
4. Ensure dependencies are installed in venv:
   - `google-genai` (required by `labs/lab1/src/app.py`)
   - `pyyaml` (required by `labs/lab2/tests/test_batch_runner.py`)
5. Ensure Node.js 22.22.0 is installed at `.venv/node-v22.22.0-linux-x64/bin/node`
6. Ensure Promptfoo 0.123.1 is at `.venv/node-tools/node_modules/promptfoo/dist/src/main.js`
7. Run: `.venv/bin/python tools/student_replay.py --lab lab1 --runtime "$REPLAY_ENV"`

## Pitfalls

- `ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'google'` means `google-genai` is not installed in `.venv`
- `ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'yaml'` means `pyyaml` is missing
- `ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'course_llm'` means `PYTHONPATH` doesn't include the source root (`/home/angel/Documents/Cyber_IA/`)
- `offline_replay.py` needs `sys.argv[2]` (work dir) in `sys.path` because `-I` ignores `PYTHONPATH`
- `Local Node 22.22.0 is missing` requires downloading and extracting `node-v22.22.0-linux-x64.tar.xz` to `.venv/`
- `Local Promptfoo 0.123.1 is missing` requires `npm ci` with `runtime/package-lock.json`

